@@ -130,6 +130,25 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spc-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes its specialties from the other side. Each specialty is shown under the name it is stored with, together with the veterinarians who hold it. A veterinarian is named in full, given name before family name. Every specialty appears, whether or not anyone holds it, and the veterinarians holding none are gathered under a group of their own. The whole list is presented at once, on a single page `[REQ-SPC-001]`. The page is read-only, and it is reachable by its own address alone — nothing links to it yet (confirmed 2026-08-11).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then each is shown by its stored name with the full name of every veterinarian holding it.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is opened, then the specialty is still shown, with no veterinarian under it.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given a veterinarian who holds no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown under a group for those holding none.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given every specialty the clinic holds, when the directory is opened, then all of them are shown together, without paging.
+- `[REQ-SPC-001]` given the supported languages, when the directory is opened, then its own wording is present in each of them.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty is shown under each of them.
+2. When the clinic holds no specialties at all, the directory opens with nothing listed rather than failing.
+3. When every veterinarian holds at least one specialty, the group for those holding none is left out.
+4. Specialties, and the veterinarians within each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
